  "details": "1. Start VRChat while streaming from a vive XR Elite using Vive Streaming Hub or Vive Business Streaming (confirmed issue with both)\n\n2. Go to Settings>big settings menu>controls and the control scheme is displayed as vive wands\n\n3. The thumbstick value acts as if its a trackpad for vive wands, tiliting it in different directions controls gestures, only moving if you press in the joystick. Movement is not analog, turning is not analog, capctive touch sensors present on the joystick do not register thumbs up, grip value is determined by trigger pull, pulling the grip triggers causes your hands to open.\n\nThis is far from ideal, as the Vive XR Elite and Focus 3 Controllers should map as if they are touch controllers, as they have pretty much all of the same inputs, only lacking capactive touch sensors on the buttons, but having it on the thumbsticks. There is no way to re-map the XR Elite in Steam to work properly. Using virtual desktop, we can get a glimpse of how it SHOULD work as Virtual Desktop tricks VRChat into thinking we're using Quest Controllers, however, Virtual Desktop does not convery Facetracking or work over a direct wired connection, so its far from ideal compared to Vive Streaming Hub.\n\nPlease properly detect vive XR Elite Controllers. They can simply use the same images and inputs that correspond with the Oculus Touch Controllers. I know not many people use this hardware yet, but I feel once the facetracking module comes out, and as the software for the XR Elite gets more refined, it will likely start to see more users.",
